<details><summary>Delete mistaken / duplicate request</summary><p>This removes the request from active lists and reports. It retains the record, attachments and audit history for the administrator. Unsent queued notifications are cancelled; already-sent emails cannot be recalled.</p><form method="post" data-confirm="Delete this request from active records? Please confirm you opened the correct request."><?php csrf();?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="delete_request"><input type="hidden" name="id" value="<?=$r['id']?>"><?php field('reason','Reason for deletion','textarea');?><button class="danger-button">Delete request</button></form></details>
<?php else:?><p>This request has been deleted from active records. Its original details are retained for audit.</p><?php endif;?>
<h2>Email delivery for this request</h2><p>Queued: awaiting the mail worker. Failed: the mail transport rejected the attempt. Sent: accepted by the server mail transport; this does not confirm inbox delivery. Superseded: cancelled before retry/deletion.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Recipient</th><th>Subject</th><th>Status</th><th>Attempts</th><th>Last sent</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach(requestNotificationRows((int)$r['id'])as $mail):?><tr><td><?=e($mail['recipient'])?></td><td><?=e($mail['subject'])?></td><td><?=e($mail['status'])?></td><td><?=(int)$mail['attempts']?></td><td><?=e($mail['sent_at']??'—')?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table></div>
